module gunbc.witness_quarantine

data witness_quarantine_authority_note: String = "THE single function-grain authority for the hermetic known-red witness quarantine. One row per (entry, function) that is RED BY DESIGN on main, carrying its own reason and dissolve_on. Both consumers derive from it: gunbc.ci_layer_roots known_red_probe_roster() projects the falsifier probe batch's ScheduleWitnessEntry roster, and v2.workflow.floor_discovery_producer drops exactly these rows from per-PR discovery via witness_quarantine_covers. It replaces the DUAL REPRESENTATION this repo carried until 2026-08-03: a path-substring WitnessExclusionRow classified QuarantineProbeExpectRed (which removed the whole FILE from discovery) plus a probe_red(entry, f) roster row (which enrolled one FUNCTION on the probe cadence) — two rows for one fact, kept aligned by the witness_exclusion_explicit_roster_rows_consistent reconciliation check rather than by construction (DESIGN 5: validation standing where construction was available). The two representations also disagreed in GRAIN, and that disagreement had a measured price: a green sibling authored into a quarantined file was excluded with it and then refused as UnexecutedDeferredWitness, so the only two ways out were splitting the file or downgrading its classification to OfflineLocalRecipe and stating the downgrade in prose — the receipt is the self_host_03_normalize_behavioral_witness_test.dag exclusion row, whose reason reads `QuarantineProbeExpectRed on the file would orphan that sibling`. At exact grain that trade does not exist: quarantining a function says nothing about its siblings, so they stay per-PR discovered. Adding a row here is the whole admission; there is no second place to edit and no alignment left to check. Dissolve-on: each row deletes in the change that greens its witness (the counted un-quarantine event of std.witness_admission), and the roster empties when the last one does."

type WitnessQuarantineRow {
  entry: String
  function: String
  reason: String
  dissolve_on: String
}

